= Finding the equation of a curve

A curve has gradient function $(d y)/(d x) = 8x - 2x^( -2 )$.

$ (d y)/(d x) &= 8x - 2x^( -2 ) \
  y &= 4x ^2 + 2x^(-1) + c \
  1 &= 4(1/2)^2 + 2(1/2)^(-1) + c \
  1 &= 1 + 4 + c \
  c &= -4 \ \

  therefore y &= 4x^2 + 2x^(-1) + c
